 1.1 By [F1], choose an open trivializing cover of $M$. Compactness gives a finite subcover $(U_i)_{i=1}^s$ with corresponding equivariant charts $P|_{U_i}\cong U_i\times SU(N)$. [F1, given, construct]
 
+1.2 In each product chart, write a point as $(x,g)$ and a tangent vector as $(v,W)$, with $W\in T_gSU(N)$. Define $\omega_i(v,W)=g^{-1}W$. This is smooth and $\mathfrak{su}(N)$-valued because left translation identifies $T_gSU(N)$ with $T_eSU(N)=\mathfrak{su}(N)$. The matrix exponential satisfies $\exp(tX)=I+tX+O(t^2)$, so the vertical curve $g\exp(tX)$ has tangent $gX$ and $\omega_i(X_P)=X$. For fixed $h\in SU(N)$, right multiplication sends $W$ to $Wh$, and $(gh)^{-1}(Wh)=h^{-1}(g^{-1}W)h$; hence $R_h^*\omega_i=\operatorname{Ad}_{h^{-1}}\omega_i$. [F1, given, construct, algebra]
